# Deliberately NOT `* text=auto`.
#
# That would renormalise every file in the repo in one commit, and this checkout
# is shared with another agent mid-work. The line-ending warnings on every commit
# are cosmetic and stay.
#
# What is here is the case that is not cosmetic: files whose bytes are the point.
# assets/posecode-embed-0.1.0.js carries its own sha256 in a comment on
# player-animations.html, and git's text detection would hand a Windows clone a
# CRLF copy that no longer matches the hash the page publishes. The tensors and
# the font are binary in fact; saying so keeps any future heuristic from deciding
# otherwise.

assets/posecode-embed-0.1.0.js         -text
public/assets/posecode-embed-0.1.0.js  -text

*.f32    -text
*.bin    -text
*.woff2  -text
*.png    -text
*.ico    -text
